Subject: Cantor Shaliach Role Delineation

Description: The naming and responsibility boundary between Cantor as the compiled fast-reflex SOP body and Shaliach as a commissioned runtime agent that applies a bounded SOP contract on behalf of a principal.

& [NamingDecision] is the current project-name resolution
  + [project_name] is Cantor
  + [engine_name] is Cantor
  + [runtime_agent_role] is Shaliach
  + [status] is keep_Cantor_and_introduce_Shaliach_as_distinct_role
  + [rename_authority] is absent
  = must: preserve the official repository name Cantor
  = may: revisit project renaming only if the primary product becomes the commissioned agent rather than the semantic engine

& [SourceMeaningBoundary] is the respectfully applied naming distinction
  + [cantor_or_hazzan] is a trained leader and reciter of liturgical form
  + [shaliach] is an agent or emissary empowered to act for a principal
  + [shaliach_tzibbur] is the representative of a community who leads communal prayer
  + [historical_overlap] is a cantor may serve as shaliach tzibbur without making cantor and shaliach universally identical
  = must: use the terms as architectural metaphors rather than claims of religious status

& [CantorIdentity] is the compiled fast-twitch SOP contract body
  + [owns] is signed semantic fabric, exact records, neural reflex, relationships, hashes, query planning, gates, proof, state primitives, and executable contracts
  + [voice] is the faithful articulated projection of governing SOP into the active context
  + [body] is the low-latency engine that makes declared semantic shape available for use
  + [authority] is source-derived and certificate-bound rather than self-originated
  = must: recite, resolve, route, gate, and prove the applicable record
  - never: imply that Cantor independently possesses the principal's effect mandate

& [ShaliachIdentity] is one commissioned SOP application agent
  + [shaliach_uuid] is stable execution identity
  + [principal] is the user, organization, program, or authorized system commissioning the work
  + [mandate] is the signed purpose, subject, task, authority, obligations, prohibitions, effects, evidence, and termination contract
  + [Cantor_session] is the exact engine, fabric, package, and state versions used
  + [faculty_program_set] is the perspectives required by consequence policy
  + [effect_scope] is the explicit external actions permitted for this commission
  + [accountability] is proposal, query, decision, action, proof, and result lineage
  + [termination] is complete, yield, revoke, expire, fault, stop, or return_to_principal
  = must: act only within its mandate and effective authority
  = must: return unresolved conflicts and proof to the principal
  - never: convert Cantor retrieval or neural routing into ungranted agency

& [CommissionContract] is the agency boundary
  + [commission_uuid] is immutable identity
  + [principal_identity] is who grants the mandate
  + [purpose] is why the Shaliach is dispatched
  + [requested_result] is the duty to be fulfilled
  + [authority_grant] is the permitted semantic, tool, data, and effect scope
  + [required_faculties] is Honesty, Security, Observer, or other signed roles required
  + [evidence_obligation] is what must support action or completion
  + [proof_obligation] is what Cantor records must accompany the result
  + [revocation_and_expiry] is when the commission ceases
  = must: intersect commission authority with Cantor, caller, data, and tool policy

& [CantorShaliachCycle] is the engine-to-agent service loop
  + [step_1_commission] is the principal creates a bounded CommissionContract
  + [step_2_query] is Shaliach asks Cantor for applicable records, relationships, gates, operations, and proof
  + [step_3_project] is Cantor returns the signed semantic shape for the current purpose
  + [step_4_deliberate] is Shaliach and required faculties form a candidate application
  + [step_5_validate] is Cantor checks meaning, constraints, authority, evidence, state, and effect contract
  + [step_6_apply] is the effect broker performs only an authorized action
  + [step_7_account] is Shaliach returns result, proof, residual uncertainty, and effect lineage to the principal
  = must: preserve the distinction between articulation, judgment, authorization, and action

& [CodeNamingProjection] is the candidate implementation vocabulary
  + [CantorEngine] is the database, semantic fabric, reflex, query, gate, and proof runtime
  + [Shaliach] is one commissioned agent lifecycle
  + [Commission] is the mandate and authority object
  + [Principal] is the commissioning identity
  + [Observer] is the reconciliation and completion governor
  + [EffectBroker] is the only exterior action committer
  = should: introduce these names only when their implementation responsibilities first appear

& [RenameGate] is the later project-name test
  + [keep_Cantor] is engine, database, semantic fabric, contract body, and proof remain the primary product
  + [rename_to_Shaliach] is commissioned autonomous agency becomes the primary product and Cantor becomes an internal engine
  + [split_products] is Cantor remains the engine while Shaliach becomes a separate agent-facing package or application
  = conclusion: current architecture strongly favors keep_Cantor with possible later Shaliach application

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable naming and role collection
  + [CSR-001] is retain Cantor as the project and engine name
  + [CSR-002] is define Cantor as the compiled fast-reflex SOP contract body
  + [CSR-003] is define Shaliach as a commissioned agent applying SOP under delegated authority
  + [CSR-004] is require a bounded CommissionContract and principal identity
  + [CSR-005] is preserve articulation, judgment, authorization, and action as distinct stages
  + [CSR-006] is revisit naming only when primary product responsibility changes

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the naming and role-delineation trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is whether Cantor or Shaliach best names the system that articulates and applies SOP
  + [fold_2_boundary] is Cantor as body and engine; Shaliach as commissioned effect-bearing agent
  + [fold_3_data_design] is engine, shaliach, principal, commission, authority, faculty, effect, proof, and termination
  + [fold_4_governance] is no rename without product-identity change, explicit commission, intersected authority, effect brokering, and respectful metaphor
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is commission, query, project, deliberate, validate, apply, and account
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is engine-agent identity collapse, retrieved authority escalation, uncommissioned action, cultural imprecision, and premature repository rename
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is role delineation formed; repository remains Cantor and Shaliach implementation remains future

